  legal: {"back":"Back to the portal","updated":"Last updated: {{date}}","privacyLink":"Privacy policy","termsLink":"Terms of use","privacy":{"title":"Privacy policy","sections":[{"h":"1. Who we are","p":["The AKAB portal (the “Portal”) is run by AKAB Informatique (“AKAB”, “we”), a managed IT services provider in Québec, Canada. This policy explains what information the Portal handles, why, and how we protect it. We follow Québec's private sector privacy law (Law 25) and PIPEDA."]},{"h":"2. What the Portal does","p":["The Portal is used to manage technical support, tickets, timesheets, invoicing and communication between AKAB and its clients. It is used by AKAB's team and, by invitation, by its clients' contacts."]},{"h":"3. Information we handle","p":["Account: name, email, phone, role, language, sign-in and activity logs.","Support: tickets, messages, notes, attachments, time worked, the client's devices and contracts.","Billing: clients, contacts, contracts, invoices, payments, vendors and the chart of accounts.","Technical: IP address, browser type and an audit log of administrative actions."]},{"h":"4. QuickBooks Online connection","p":["With the permission of an AKAB administrator, the Portal connects to QuickBooks Online (Intuit) using OAuth 2.0 with the “Accounting” scope only.","Data read or written in QuickBooks: customers, vendors, chart of accounts, items and categories, invoices and payments. Nothing else is requested.","Why: to keep customers, the chart of accounts and the chosen vendors up to date, send invoices made in the Portal, and bring back their payment status.","Access tokens are encrypted in our database and are never shown or sent to the browser. We do not sell this data, do not share it for advertising, and use it only to run this connection.","You can disconnect QuickBooks at any time in the Portal (Administration › Integrations › QuickBooks) or by removing the app in your Intuit account. After disconnecting, the Portal exchanges nothing with QuickBooks. Data already copied into the Portal stays there (see “Retention”).","Use of QuickBooks is also subject to Intuit's terms and privacy statement. AKAB is not affiliated with Intuit."]},{"h":"5. Other services we use","p":["Depending on setup: Microsoft 365 (each technician's mail and calendar, through their own sign-in), Stripe (card payments), a text-message provider, an artificial intelligence provider for writing and planning help, and a mail server. Each receives only what its function needs."]},{"h":"6. How we use information","p":["We use information to provide the service, support clients, invoice, secure accounts and meet legal duties. We do not sell personal information and do not use advertising trackers."]},{"h":"7. Sharing","p":["Information is shared only with the service providers needed to run the Portal (hosting, email, payment, accounting), with the client concerned, or when the law requires it."]},{"h":"8. Security","p":["Strong passwords and two-factor sign-in, server-side sessions, role-based access, encrypted integration keys, HTTPS, and an audit log of administrative actions. No system is perfect: if an incident affects personal information we will notify the people concerned and the authorities as the law requires."]},{"h":"9. Retention","p":["We keep information as long as needed to provide the service and meet accounting and legal requirements (for example, keeping invoices). On request, we delete or anonymize what no longer has to be kept."]},{"h":"10. Your rights","p":["You may ask for access to your information, its correction or deletion, withdraw a consent, or ask about our practices. Write to us at the address below. You may also contact the Commission d'accès à l'information du Québec."]},{"h":"11. Cookies","p":["The Portal uses one session cookie needed to sign in. There is no advertising and no tracking tool."]},{"h":"12. Changes","p":["We may update this policy. The date of the last update is at the top of the page."]},{"h":"13. Contact","p":["AKAB Informatique, 5 rue Industrielle, Saint-Roch-de-l'Achigan (Québec) J0K 3H0, Canada — 450-834-3344 — akab.ca"]}]},"terms":{"title":"Terms of use","sections":[{"h":"1. Acceptance","p":["By using the AKAB portal (the “Portal”) you accept these terms. If you do not, do not use the Portal."]},{"h":"2. The service","p":["The Portal is provided by AKAB Informatique to manage technical support, tickets, time, invoicing and communication with its clients. Available features depend on your role."]},{"h":"3. Accounts","p":["Accounts are created by invitation. Keep your credentials confidential, use two-factor sign-in where required, and tell us promptly of any unauthorized use."]},{"h":"4. Acceptable use","p":["Do not use the Portal to harm its operation, bypass security, access other people's data, or upload illegal or malicious content."]},{"h":"5. QuickBooks Online connection","p":["An AKAB administrator may link the Portal to QuickBooks Online to sync customers, chart of accounts, vendors, invoices and payments. The link needs your authorization at Intuit and can be removed at any time. Use of QuickBooks remains governed by Intuit's terms; AKAB is not affiliated with Intuit. How data is handled is described in the privacy policy."]},{"h":"6. Your data","p":["You remain the owner of your data. You allow us to process it to provide the service, as the privacy policy explains."]},{"h":"7. Availability","p":["We aim for a reliable service but do not guarantee it will be free of interruption or error. The Portal may be changed or updated."]},{"h":"8. Limit of liability","p":["To the extent the law allows, AKAB is not liable for indirect damages, lost profits or lost data arising from use of the Portal, and its total liability is limited to the amounts paid for the service in the last 12 months. These limits do not apply to what the law does not allow to be excluded."]},{"h":"9. Ending access","p":["We may suspend or close an account in case of abuse or when the relationship with the client ends. You may stop using the Portal at any time."]},{"h":"10. Governing law","p":["These terms are governed by the laws of Québec and the federal laws of Canada that apply there. The courts of Québec have jurisdiction."]},{"h":"11. Changes","p":["We may change these terms; the update date is at the top of the page. Continuing to use the Portal means you accept them."]},{"h":"12. Contact","p":["AKAB Informatique, 5 rue Industrielle, Saint-Roch-de-l'Achigan (Québec) J0K 3H0, Canada — 450-834-3344 — akab.ca"]}]}},
